### Step 2: Create `RedisPubSubConfig.java` (Create New)

You need to create a new configuration file to listen for the Redis trigger that tells the `ValidationMasterService` to refresh.

**File:** `src/main/java/com/fincore/VoucherService/config/RedisPubSubConfig.java`

```java
package com.fincore.VoucherService.config;

import com.fincore.VoucherService.Service.ValidationMasterService;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.data.redis.connection.RedisConnectionFactory;
import org.springframework.data.redis.listener.ChannelTopic;
import org.springframework.data.redis.listener.RedisMessageListenerContainer;
import org.springframework.data.redis.listener.adapter.MessageListenerAdapter;

@Configuration
public class RedisPubSubConfig {

    public static final String MASTER_DATA_TOPIC = "master-data-updates";

    @Bean
    public ChannelTopic masterDataTopic() {
        return new ChannelTopic(MASTER_DATA_TOPIC);
    }

    @Bean
    public MessageListenerAdapter masterDataListenerAdapter(ValidationMasterService validationMasterService) {
        // Tells Redis to execute the 'refreshMasterData' method when a message arrives
        return new MessageListenerAdapter(validationMasterService, "refreshMasterData");
    }

    @Bean
    public RedisMessageListenerContainer masterDataRedisContainer(RedisConnectionFactory connectionFactory,
                                                        MessageListenerAdapter masterDataListenerAdapter,
                                                        ChannelTopic masterDataTopic) {
        RedisMessageListenerContainer container = new RedisMessageListenerContainer();
        container.setConnectionFactory(connectionFactory);
        container.addMessageListener(masterDataListenerAdapter, masterDataTopic);
        return container;
    }
}

```

